# ---------------- Part 7: Fills ----------------

C(86, 7, 'What Is a Fill?', 'Leading the band into the next section',
  P('A <b>fill</b> is a short break from the groove that leads into the next part of a song. Fills usually come at the end of a phrase (every 4 or 8 bars) and land on a crash cymbal with the bass drum on beat 1.'),
  P('A fill should take up <b>exactly</b> the same time as the groove it replaces. The most common mistake is rushing.'),
  E('One bar of groove, one bar of fill', 'The fill is four quarter notes around the kit. Listen for the crash when it loops back to the top.', bars=2, bpm=84,
    lines=dict(cr='x... .... .... ....', hh='.xxx xxxx .... ....', sn='..o. ..o. o... ....', t1='.... .... ..o. ....', t2='.... .... .... o.o.', bd='o... o... o... o...')),
  TIP('Count the phrase', 'Count bars out loud while you play: “1-2-3-4, 2-2-3-4, 3-2-3-4, FILL-2-3-4”. You’ll always know when the fill is coming.'),
),

