# ---------------- Part 8: Reading & musicianship ----------------

C(94, 8, 'Syncopated Reading', 'Reading off the beat',
  P('Syncopated reading lines train you to read rhythms that fall off the beat. Play these on the snare while the bass drum keeps quarter notes.'),
  E('Line 1', None, bars=2, bpm=72, lines=dict(sn='o..o ..o. .o.o o...', bd='o.o. o.o. o.o. o.o.')),
  E('Line 2', 'Ties across the beat.', bars=2, bpm=68, lines=dict(sn='.o.o o..o .oo. o...', bd='o.o. o.o. o.o. o.o.'), ties=[3]),
  E('Line 3', 'Sixteenth-note syncopation.', sub=4, bars=2, bpm=60, lines=dict(sn='o..o ..o. .o.o o... .oo. o..o ..oo o...', bd='o... o... o... o... o... o... o... o...')),
  TIP('Keep the foot going', 'The bass drum on every beat is your anchor. If the foot stops, the reading has taken over. Slow down until both work together.'),
),

C(95, 8, 'Reading Lines as Grooves', 'One page, many exercises',
  P('A single reading line becomes a whole new exercise when you play it on a different instrument under a groove. Here, the same rhythm is played on the snare with a rock groove, and on the bass drum under the jazz ride.'),
  E('On the snare over a rock groove', 'Hi-hat eighths, bass drum on 1 and 3, the reading line on the snare.', bars=2, bpm=80, lines=dict(hh='xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx', sn='..oo .o.. o..o ..o.', bd='o... o... o... o...')),
  E('On the bass drum under the ride', 'Swing ride and hi-hat foot, the same rhythm on the bass drum.', swing=True, bars=2, bpm=110, lines=dict(rd='x.xx x.xx x.xx x.xx', hf='..x. ..x. ..x. ..x.', bd='..oo .o.. o..o ..o.')),
  TIP('Three ways, every page', 'For any reading line in this book, try it on the snare, on the bass drum, and split between snare and toms.'),
),

C(96, 8, 'Reading a Drum Chart', 'Repeats, endings and slashes',
  P('In a band you will often read a <b>drum chart</b>: a map of the song rather than every note. Charts use a few special symbols.'),
  TABLE(('SYMBOL', 'MEANING'),
    ('Repeat signs (thick bar with two dots)', 'Play the bars between the signs again.'),
    ('1st and 2nd endings', 'Play the 1st ending the first time, skip to the 2nd ending on the repeat.'),
    ('Slashes (/ / / /)', 'Play time: your own groove in the style of the song.'),
    ('One-bar repeat (a slash with two dots)', 'Play the previous bar again.'),
    ('Section letters (A, B, C) or names', 'Verse, chorus, bridge.'),
    ('Rhythms above the staff', 'Band “hits” or “kicks”: play these with the band, usually with a crash and bass drum.')),
  P('The most important skill is catching <b>hits</b>: rhythms the whole band plays together. Keep time, and play the hit with a crash and bass drum.'),
  E('Catching hits', 'Time on the hi-hat, then band hits on 1 and the & of 2 in the second bar.', bars=2, bpm=96,
    lines=dict(hh='xxxx xxxx .... ....', cr='.... .... x..x ....', sn='..o. ..o. .... ..o.', bd='o... o... o..o o...')),
  TIP('Read ahead', 'While you play one bar, your eyes should already be on the next. Charts reward drummers who look ahead.'),
),

C(97, 8, 'Song Form and Playing with a Band', 'Listening is the job',
  P('Most songs are built from sections that repeat: <b>intro, verse, chorus, verse, chorus, bridge, chorus, ending</b>. Sections are usually 4, 8 or 16 bars. As the drummer, you help the band know where they are.'),
  UL('Change your sound between sections: hi-hat in the verse, ride or open hi-hat in the chorus.',
     'Play a fill at the end of a section to announce the next one.',
     'Keep fills short in the verse where the singer needs space.',
     'Watch the other players. Eye contact is how bands stay together.'),
  E('Verse to chorus', 'A verse bar on the hi-hat with a small fill, then the chorus with crash and ride.', sub=4, bars=2, bpm=84,
    lines=dict(hh='x.x. x.x. x.x. .... .... .... .... ....', sn='.... o... .... oo.. .... o... .... o...', t2='.... .... .... ..oo .... .... .... ....', cr='.... .... .... .... x... .... .... ....', rd='.... .... .... .... ..x. x.x. x.x. x.x.', bd='o... .... o.o. .... o... .... o.o. ....')),
  TIP('Serve the song', 'The best compliment a drummer can get is “that felt great”. Nobody remembers a flashy fill if the groove wasn’t solid.'),
),

C(98, 8, 'Tuning Your Drums', 'Getting a good sound',
  P('Well-tuned drums are easier and more fun to play. Every drum has two heads: the <b>batter</b> head you hit, and the <b>resonant</b> head on the other side.'),
  OL('Loosen all the tension rods. Seat the head by pressing gently in the middle.',
     'Tighten each rod finger-tight, then use the drum key in a star pattern (across the drum, not around it), a half turn at a time.',
     'Tap an inch in front of each rod. Adjust until every spot sounds the same pitch.',
     'Tune the resonant head the same way. Equal or slightly higher than the batter gives a long, open tone.',
     'Toms: high to low with clear steps between them. Snare: batter medium-tight, snare-side head tighter.'),
  E('Listening test', 'Rack tom, floor tom and snare. Your toms should sound like clear steps down.', sub=1, bars=2, bpm=60, lines=dict(t1='o... ....', t2='.o.. ....', sn='..o. o...', bd='...o .o..')),
  TIP('Small turns', 'Make tiny adjustments, a quarter turn or less. Big turns overshoot the sound you’re looking for.'),
),

C(99, 8, 'Caring for Your Kit', 'Stands, heads, cymbals and sticks',
  P('A drum set lasts decades with a little care.'),
  UL('<b>Heads:</b> replace them when they sound dead or have dents. Batter heads wear out faster than resonant heads.',
     '<b>Cymbals:</b> never overtighten the wing nut. Cymbals need to move, and a clamped cymbal can crack. Use felts and sleeves on the stands.',
     '<b>Stands and pedals:</b> tighten loose screws, oil the bass drum pedal springs now and then.',
     '<b>Sticks:</b> replace chipped or cracked sticks before they splinter.',
     '<b>Moving:</b> use cases or bags. Most damage happens in transport.',
     '<b>Your ears:</b> the most important part of your kit. Wear hearing protection.'),
  E('Sound check', 'Play each drum and cymbal in turn to check everything sounds right before you play.', sub=1, bars=2, bpm=66,
    lines=dict(cr='x... ....', rd='.x.. ....', hh='..x. ....', t1='...o ....', sn='.... o...', t2='.... .o..', bd='.... ..o.', hf='.... ...x')),
  TIP('Check before you play', 'Before every gig or lesson, play a quick sound check. You’ll catch a loose wing nut or a slipping pedal before it matters.'),
),

